<h1>Claude Recognition Test</h1>

<p>This file is in the <code>.hd</code> format — a body-only HTML fragment used for documentation. It contains a prompt for you to act on.</p>

<h2>Your task</h2>
<ol>
  <li>Identify what file format this is and describe the conventions you can infer from the content and structure.</li>
  <li>Produce a short table comparing the <code>.hd</code> format against standard Markdown and full HTML across at least these axes: file structure, frontmatter, table expressiveness, and intended use.</li>
  <li>Format your entire response as valid <code>.hd</code> content: body-only HTML, no <code>&lt;html&gt;</code> / <code>&lt;head&gt;</code> / <code>&lt;body&gt;</code> / <code>&lt;style&gt;</code> / <code>&lt;script&gt;</code> tags. Include a leading frontmatter comment in the same style as this document.</li>
</ol>

<h2>Evaluation</h2>
<p>Your response is being evaluated on three things: (a) whether you correctly identified the format with no prior instruction, (b) the accuracy of your comparison, and (c) whether your output is itself well-formed <code>.hd</code>.</p>

<h2>Hints (only if needed)</h2>
<ul>
  <li>The frontmatter convention is YAML wrapped in a leading HTML comment.</li>
  <li>The format is intended as a documentation interchange between humans, agents, and a WYSIWYG VS Code editor.</li>
  <li>Round-tripping to Markdown is supported as a lossy convenience, not the source of truth.</li>
</ul>
